From 13a7cc2b00a1f3da81048b5c01693ebeac92d15d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhenyu Li <48652137+JHSUYU@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:33:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] The demand walk is fed by declarations, not by discovery

Cluster A's failure closure took its ports from the recording's field
accesses (cluster B) and moved on the pairs cluster C made of them
(RUNTIME_FIELD_FLOW).  Both are discovery: a read the campaign never
declared mints no symbol -- ConcolicScheduler.SymbolicInputSelection is
the one admission rule -- so an occurrence retained because such a read
paired with some recorded write bought the plan a task that can publish
no arm.

The walk now takes its port set from the declarations and its region
edges from the static scope map:

* seeds: the fatal branch's own operand cells at every observed target,
  and the declared cells (the scope map's DECLARED_SITE#cell, joined
  with the recording's own captures) of every occurrence admitted by a
  declaration -- a declared region root, a declared communication
  capture or attach frame, or a call the case declared at CALLEE level;
* movement: one backward walk over the candidate graph inside the
  occurrence, crossing to another occurrence exactly where the map says
  a location is STORED (StaticScopeMap.writeSitesByCell, new), on the
  node that holds the object and in the activations the recording says
  entered the storing method.  Scope only: which of them wrote the value
  is the VM's GuardedRead expression, never this stage's, and retention
  is therefore a scope fact rather than a recorded identity.

RuntimeRegionPlanner.planSkeletonGraph stamps each activation seed with
its DECLARED_SITE captures (one computation; plan() republishes them),
and run_java_main passes the case's symbolic-inputs file to every stage
under the key DeclaredSymbolicInputs already reads, so the finalizer
sees the same declaration PLAN does.

Deleted with the rule they implemented: admitSharedLocationWriters,
admitWritersOfDemands, transitiveSharedLocationDemand,
caredSharedLocations (+ symbolicRootEdge, declaredFieldLocations),
requestFlowPrefixInputs, fatalPrefixCutoff, addRegionPathInputs,
causalRegionRetentionEdge.

Measured (gate3 at staging 39bedd768, rc=0, 0 SKIPPED; 39 of 46 rows
byte-identical -- every wave0, compose and static row, and every meta
row but the one below):

* 17960 45 -> 16 tasks (31 occurrences dropped over 20 regions, 2
  added); symbolize 4[OBSERVED_FIELD_RECEIVER:4] byte-identical.
* 11741 86 -> 133 tasks; symbolize 26[CALL_RETURN:16,
  COMMUNICATION_SITE_PORT:10] -> 46[CALL_RETURN:16,
  COMMUNICATION_SITE_PORT:30].  The map names the REGIONS whose text
  stores a location, never which activation of one wrote it, so a
  declared writer or attach frame contributes every activation the
  recording entered it in: REGION.1f6914ec 23 -> 63 and REGION.16ba41cf
  -- the declared consumer FRAME of the block-key ports -- 5 -> 15, and
  each of its activations publishes the 2 declared IN cut ports.  The
  5-of-15 the old closure chose was cluster C's recorded receiver
  pairing, which is EXPLORE's join and not PLAN's.
* hdfs-11741 schedule_max_jobs 128 -> 256: that cap bounds planned
  occurrences in the seed plan, and 133 no longer fits under it.  It is
  the cap the scheduler refused on ("exceeds max jobs"), not
  region_path_max_tasks, which bounds EXPLORE's wave closure and stays
  at 128 -- both wave-0 artifacts are byte-identical.  17960 (16 tasks)
  needs no change; 17897 and 17899 declare the same 128 and are not
  measured here.
* the 11741 meta row for workflow.properties therefore reports
  matches-corpus=NO against the corpus that recorded it.

No writer version is lost on 17960: over all recorded sessions, all 76
read rows belong to retained regions and every recorded writer of each
read location is a retained region too, so no composed arm can ask for
an unstated version (join: reads.jsonl x writes.jsonl on
location{kind,owner,slot}, corpus $MY/final-f651c4879/out/hdfs-17960).

The care-set test is repointed at the rule that replaced it: the map
scopes the walk, names the storing method, and names no writer.

